---
title: llm-architectures TPU orchestration — layers and what each survives
---
flowchart TD
    subgraph L1["Layer 1 — Claude session (disposable)"]
        CS["reads logs, decides, edits code<br/>NEVER owns a long loop"]
    end

    subgraph L2["Layer 2 — Workstation tmux (survives Claude)"]
        QW["qrwatch<br/>scripts/tpu/qr_watch.sh<br/>/tmp/qr_watch.log"]
        SW["sweep<br/>scripts/tpu/sweep_runner.sh<br/>/tmp/sweep_runner.log"]
    end

    subgraph L3["Layer 3 — QR metadata (survives node reboot)"]
        MD["code-tarball-uri<br/>resume-from-step=auto<br/>W&B run identity"]
    end

    subgraph L4["Layer 4 — VM tmux 'train' (survives workstation)"]
        W0["worker 0<br/>/tmp/train.log"]
        WN["workers 1..15<br/>/tmp/train.log"]
    end

    subgraph L5["Layer 5 — External (survives everything)"]
        GCS["GCS<br/>checkpoints + code tarball"]
        WB["W&B<br/>metrics"]
        NT["ntfy.sh<br/>push events"]
    end

    CS -.reads.-> QW
    CS -.reads.-> SW
    SW -->|deploy_tarball.sh| W0
    SW -->|--worker=all| WN
    QW -->|recycle on preemption| MD
    MD -->|boot self-heal| W0
    W0 <-->|jax.distributed rendezvous| WN
    W0 --> GCS
    W0 --> WB
    QW --> NT
    SW --> NT

    classDef ephemeral fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#856404
    classDef durable fill:#d4edda,stroke:#155724
    class CS ephemeral
    class GCS,WB,NT durable
